<urn:architecture:image-annotation-tool:commit:1e415ac8413eb9e53fd1e596e04e3bb446097b15> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Ontology: publish the C4 architecture ontology, Turtle export, lossless RDF round trip" .
<urn:architecture:image-annotation-tool:commit:1e415ac8413eb9e53fd1e596e04e3bb446097b15> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#endedAtTime> "2026-11-19T15:43:27Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
<urn:architecture:image-annotation-tool:commit:1e415ac8413eb9e53fd1e596e04e3bb446097b15> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasAssociatedWith> <urn:architecture:image-annotation-tool:agent:caviri> .
<urn:architecture:image-annotation-tool:commit:1e415ac8413eb9e53fd1e596e04e3bb446097b15> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://github.com/caviri/c4-model-agentic-plugin/commit/1e415ac8413eb9e53fd1e596e04e3bb446097b15> .
<urn:architecture:image-annotation-tool:commit:1e415ac8413eb9e53fd1e596e04e3bb446097b15> <https://caviri.github.io/c4-model-agentic-plugin/ontology/c4-history#sha> "1e415ac8413eb9e53fd1e596e04e3bb446097b15" .
<urn:architecture:image-annotation-tool:commit:1e415ac8413eb9e53fd1e596e04e3bb446097b15> <https://caviri.github.io/c4-model-agentic-plugin/ontology/c4-history#parentSha> "d89f0dd037251d898e72d4a8055810f8050aa1cd" .
<urn:architecture:image-annotation-tool:commit:1e415ac8413eb9e53fd1e596e04e3bb446097b15> <https://caviri.github.io/c4-model-agentic-plugin/ontology/c4-history#message> "Ontology: publish the C4 architecture ontology, Turtle export, lossless RDF round trip\n\nAdd ontology/ with c4.ttl (the architecture: people, systems, containers,\ndata stores, components, code, relationships, scenarios and steps,\nstates and transitions, use cases), c4-view.ttl (how the explorer draws\nit), c4-shapes.ttl (SHACL every exported graph meets), alignments.ttl,\na README, EXTENDING.md with good practices, and a worked deployment\nextension. The namespace moves from urn:arch-explorer:vocab# to\nhttps://caviri.github.io/c4-model-agentic-plugin/ontology/c4#.\n\nThe graph is now a complete description of every explorer diagram:\npositions, view defaults, legend and level names are exported, and\narchRdf.fromTriples rebuilds the model from N-Triples, Turtle or\nJSON-LD. build-explorer.mjs can build a page from a graph alone, and\ncheck-roundtrip.mjs proves the page and screenshots are identical.\n\nScenarios gain use-case fields (actor, goal, trigger, preconditions,\noutcome), filled for two example scenarios from the code. Turtle is\noffered in the export menu, the editor and every build. A model can\ncarry its own extension terms through an rdf hook. The docs site gains\nan Ontology section with generated term pages and serves the .ttl files." .
